 "manufacturer": "Advanced Monolithic Systems",
 "title": "AMS1117: 1 A three-terminal low-dropout regulator, adjustable or fixed 1.5 V to 5.0 V",
 "source": {
  "document": "DS1117",
  "revision": "",
  "pages": 8
 },
 "summary": "A three-terminal positive linear regulator rated for 1 A, with a dropout of 1.1 V typical and 1.3 V at most at 0.8 A. One version sets its output with two resistors against a 1.25 V reference between OUT and ADJ; six fixed versions give 1.5, 1.8, 2.5, 2.85, 3.3 or 5.0 V. Current limiting and thermal shutdown protect it, and it needs an output capacitor for stability (22 µF tantalum covers every case). It comes in SOT-223, TO-252 and 8-lead SOIC, all rated for a junction of -40 °C to 125 °C.",
 "key_figures": [
  [
