   "title": "Adjustable regulator with output-to-input diode (Figure 1)",
   "page": 4,
   "description": "The adjustable part set by a divider: R1 from VOUT to ADJ, R2 from ADJ to ground. CADJ bypasses the adjust node for better ripple rejection, and a 22 µF tantalum holds the output stable. D1, anode on the output and cathode on the input, carries the output capacitor's charge back to the input if the input is shorted, as by a crowbar.",
